      "shell": "/usr/bin/osascript -l JavaScript -e 'var s = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.applicationaccess\"); (ObjC.unwrap(s.objectForKey(\"allowCloudPhotoLibrary\")) == false && s.objectIsForcedForKey(\"allowCloudPhotoLibrary\")) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"'"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The built-in Photos.app's connection to Apple's iCloud service _MUST_ be disabled, unless the organization has explicitly authorized the use of iCloud as a approved photo management service.\n\nApple's iCloud service does not provide an organization with enough control over the storage and access of data, and, therefore, automated photo synchronization _MUST_ be controlled by an organization approved service.\n\nThis requirement helps ensure that organizational photo data is managed in accordance with established security, privacy, access-control, and data governance requirements.\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
